     2	
     3	Discipline (RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md):
     4	
     5	- ``HARNESS_VERSION`` freezes the measurement system: observation format
     6	  (state features), action menu, and label pipeline. Any change to state
     7	  features, the ActionType menu, or any S-class supervision-defining
     8	  component (§6.6) REQUIRES a bump.
     9	- ``UTILITY_VERSION`` is the finer stamp: it tracks the S-class label
    10	  definition only (utility weights/scales, continuation policy, rollout
    11	  horizon, gold temperature, action-subset quota, replicate count).
    12	
    13	Reading rule (:func:`check_record_versions`):
    14	
    15	- ``OK``       — record carries the current stamps; poolable.
    16	- ``LEGACY``   — stamp missing (records predate the mechanism) or holds a
    17	  known-past value: readable, but must not be pooled with current-version
    18	  records without an explicit same-data A/B note (§6.6 rule 1).
    19	- ``MISMATCH`` — stamp is not a recognized value (e.g. a future version
    20	  read by older code): refuse to pool.
    21	
    22	Known-past values are listed in ``_KNOWN_PAST``; extend it when bumping
    23	either constant so old data reads as LEGACY rather than MISMATCH.
