    10	Estimands (declared before running).
    11	
    12	  Model:  y_{f,s,L} = mu + alpha_f + beta_{c(f,L)} + error, where
    13	          L in LEVELS = {5, 8, 12, 18} (raw n_init) and
    14	          c(f,L) = L / (2 d_f + 1)  is the dimension-relative design size
    15	          (the axis recommended by the screen report: raw n_init means
    16	          different things at different d).
    17	  Reference level: L0 = 5 (harness default).
    18	  Per-family contrast:      Delta_{f,L} = E_s[y_{f,s,L} - y_{f,s,L0}].
    19	  Per-family dose slope:    b_f = E_s[b_{f,s}], where b_{f,s} is the OLS
    20	                            slope of y_{f,s,·} on c over the 4 levels
    21	                            (seed-paired; levels share the Sobol prefix).
    22	  H0_slope : the REFERENCE-STANDARDIZED slopes b_f / sd_ref(f) are equal
    23	             across families (common dose response — no family x dose
    24	             interaction). PRIMARY test. Standardization by each family's
    25	             reference-level sd makes the test invariant to per-family
    26	             objective rescaling (scale-stable; codex round-3 D1); raw-unit
    27	             slopes are reported secondarily.
    28	  H0_pair  : Delta_{f,12} identical across families (direct comparability
    29	             with the screen). SECONDARY.
    30	  Mechanistic (directional, predeclared): multimodal families (Rastrigin,
    31	  Ackley) have b_f > 0; smooth families (Branin, Hartmann, SixHumpCamel)
    32	  have b_f < 0.
    33	
    34	Design.
    35	
    36	  - LEVELS = {5, 8, 12, 18}; budget 30 evaluations (design + BO) for all
    37	    levels; pinned AlwaysSurrogate policy; same family + seed -> same
    38	    scrambled Sobol stream with the prefix property across levels.
    39	  - Seeds 0..59 (60): seeds 0-19 replicate the screen's sample exactly
    40	    (nested), 20-59 are NEW — the replication/confirmation split is
    41	    seeds 0-19 (discovery, prior sample) vs 20-59 (confirmation, fresh).
    42	  - 5 families x 4 levels x 60 seeds = 1200 trajectories.
    43	
    44	Inference.
