     1	"""EXP-META-CONFIG-SCREEN — meta-level config-conditionality screen (guide §5.2/§10.3).
     2	
     3	Research question. Before building any meta-level supervision pipeline, is
     4	there detectable CONFIGURATION-CONDITIONALITY on the current panel — i.e.,
     5	does the advantage of one design-phase configuration over another depend on
     6	the problem family? Guide §4.4 warns the meta-level advantage may be
     7	nonpositive everywhere; this screen is the cheap paired test the round-1
     8	review (E2) asked for.
     9	
    10	Estimands (declared before running).
    11	
    12	  Model:  y_{f,s,a} = mu + alpha_f + beta_a + (alpha beta)_{f,a} + eps_{f,s,a}
    13	          f = family (1..F), a in {small, large}, s = seed (paired).
    14	  Delta_f = E_s[y_{f,s,large} - y_{f,s,small}]
    15	          = (beta_large - beta_small) + (alpha beta)_{f,large} - (alpha beta)_{f,small}
    16	          is the per-family config advantage (maximization units).
    17	  H0_int : Delta_1 = ... = Delta_F  (no family x config interaction —
    18	           the best config does not vary by family).
    19	  H1_int : some Delta_f differ.
    20	
    21	  Descriptor (NOT a test statistic): meta-D = E_f[max_a u_{a,f}] -
    22	  max_a E_f[u_{a,f}] on family-standardized utilities u. In POPULATION terms
    23	  meta-D > 0 iff the Delta_f are not all of one sign; it measures the value
    24	  of an oracle that knows the family label. It says nothing about whether a
    25	  LEARNABLE problem signature could recover that oracle — for that we report
    26	  a leave-one-family-out (LOFO) sign-prediction probe as a descriptive
    27	  lower-bound diagnostic.
    28	
    29	Design.
    30	
    31	  - Config axis: initial design size n_init in {5 ("small", harness
    32	    default), 12 ("large")} — a design-phase configuration per guide §1.2.
    33	    Both arms spend the SAME total budget (default 30 evaluations,
    34	    design + BO; verified per trajectory).
    35	  - Inner policy pinned to AlwaysSurrogate in both arms (isolates the
    36	    config effect).
    37	  - Pairing: same family + same seed -> same scrambled Sobol stream; the
    38	    small arm's design is a PREFIX of the large arm's (verified in backend:
    39	    draw(n) on a fresh seeded engine).
    40	  - Endpoint: terminal best objective (backend maximizes).
    41	
    42	Mechanistic hypotheses (declared before running; directional, tested
    43	descriptively against sign(Delta_f)).
    44	
    45	  H-mech-1 (multimodality -> space-filling): strongly multimodal families
    46	  (Rastrigin, Ackley) benefit from a larger space-filling design because it
    47	  covers more local basins before LogEI commits.
    48	  H-mech-2 (smoothness -> model-guided budget): smooth families
    49	  (Branin, Hartmann, SixHumpCamel) are hurt by spending budget on design
    50	  points the GP could have placed itself (mild negative Delta_f).
    51	  Predicted sign pattern: positive on {Rastrigin, Ackley}, negative on
    52	  {Branin, Hartmann, SixHumpCamel}. We report n_init relative to the 2d+1
    53	  heuristic per family to interpret the axis.
    54	
    55	Inference (all primary tests predeclared).
    56	
    57	  1. Per family: paired mean Delta_hat_f, seed-level percentile bootstrap
    58	     CI (5000), paired t test, and Cohen's d_z = Delta_hat_f / sd(d_fs).
    59	  2. Interaction (PRIMARY): homogeneity Wald test
    60	     X^2 = sum_f (Delta_hat_f - Delta_hat_w)^2 / Var(Delta_hat_f),
    61	     Var(Delta_hat_f) = sd_f^2 / n, referenced to chi^2_{F-1}. This is the
    62	     continuous analogue of Cochran's Q and tolerates the family-scale
    63	     heterogeneity that defeats naive pooling. Heterogeneity share
    64	     I^2 = max(0, (X^2 - df) / X^2).
    65	  3. Discovery / confirmation split: seeds 0..half-1 discovery,
    66	     half..n-1 confirmation. A family is CONFIRMED iff both halves agree in
    67	     sign AND the confirmation-half bootstrap CI excludes zero.
    68	  4. Precision floor (futility semantics for a negative screen): per family
    69	     report the 80%-power minimum detectable difference MDD_f ~ 2.80 *
    70	     se_f and the CI half-width relative to 0.25 * sd_f (a declared
    71	     minimal-interesting standardized effect).
    72	
    73	Predeclared decision rules.
    74	
    75	  - CONDITIONALITY DETECTED iff interaction p < 0.05 (chi^2_{F-1}).
    76	  - Axis FUTILE (stop, per guide §5.5.4) iff NOT detected AND every
    77	    family's CI half-width < 0.25 * sd_f (precise null).
    78	  - Otherwise: INCONCLUSIVE (not detected but underpowered) — the axis is
    79	    parked, not killed.
    80	  - meta-D and LOFO are reported as descriptors and do NOT enter the rule.
    81	
    82	Hardware: CPU-bound trajectories; F x n x 2 jobs, mp.Pool with a
    83	torch single-thread initializer (oversubscription guard).
    84	"""
