codex
A read-only jackknife calculation from the saved trajectories found one more issue: the primary test treats each family’s estimated reference SD as fixed. Recomputing slope uncertainty with that SD included gives an exploratory Q≈20.8 (p≈3.5×10⁻⁴), versus the reported 38.69 (p≈8.1×10⁻⁸). Detection remains plausible, but the reported strength is overstated; I’m finishing the verdict with that distinction.
codex
## A. Round-3 dispositions

The round-3 log names **12 finding IDs**, although its summary says 13. E2 contained two distinct requirements, shown separately below to make the requested 13 checks.

| Finding | Verdict | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| A1 | ADDRESSED | Guide §6.5 says the aggregate result is consistent with, but does not establish, the unmeasured pointwise premise. |
| B1 | PARTIAL | `iter_jsonl` is documented as raw access, but training consumers still use it; `train_system1_compare` calls `read_jsonl` with its unchecked default. |
| B2 | ADDRESSED | `strict` rejects current-plus-legacy stamps within one source unless `pool_legacy=True`. |
| B3 | PARTIAL | Live table has four cells per row; the parser still accepts extra header cells and can miss a second table with a different header. |
| C1 | ADDRESSED | §5.5.2 requires a positive CI lower bound and states an equivalence bound for termination. |
| C2 | ADDRESSED | THEORY P3 now keeps the empirical reading conditional and identifies the pointwise premise as unmeasured. |
| C3 | ADDRESSED | §5.5.1 identifies replicas 0–3, excludes replica 4, and requires the pair rule to be declared after redesign. |
| D1 | PARTIAL | Code and headline use standardized slopes; the grid report, serialized estimand, and PROGRESS still call the raw-slope test primary. |
| D2 | PARTIAL | The abstract, §6.2, and PROGRESS §19 mark retraction; screen §6.3 still says only Rastrigin was significant without that qualification. |
| D3 | UNADDRESSED | Grid §8.2 still calls the selected settings an “always-usable” baseline. |
| E1 | PARTIAL | §4.5 states the boundary, but unchecked loading remains possible in pooling consumers. |
| E2a — equivalence bound | PARTIAL | The calculation changed; guide §5.5.4 and the script’s declared and serialized rules still say CI half-width. |
| E2b — all contrasts | UNADDRESSED | FUTILE still checks only each family’s selected best-versus-reference contrast and skips a family when reference wins. |

## B. New-issue and consistency check

The live §2.4 table matches the parser’s four-column shape by inspection. The saved grid artifact contains **38.69 / 0.90**; **30.87 / 0.87** is the raw-unit secondary result. The following issues prevent a PASS:

| Severity | Location and issue | One-line fix |
|---|---|---|
| MAJOR | [grid script](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/scripts/exp_meta_config_grid.py:241): the primary test treats estimated `sd_ref` as fixed when computing slope SEs. A read-only jackknife from saved trajectories gives exploratory Q≈20.8, p≈3.5×10⁻⁴, versus reported Q=38.69, p≈8.1×10⁻⁸. | Include reference-SD uncertainty through joint seed resampling or a suitable variance estimate, then refresh the statistic and reports. |
| MAJOR | [training call](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/scripts/train_system1_compare.py:74) uses `read_jsonl`’s `"allow"` default; [another training consumer](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/scripts/phase9_baselines.py:180) still uses unchecked `iter_jsonl`. | Give every pooling consumer an explicit enforcing policy and migrate remaining training and labeling paths. |
| MAJOR | [pooling check](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/src/opt_agent/dataset/versioning.py:135) sees one file and coarse status values: two separately loaded files, or two different known-past stamps, can still be combined silently; the boolean opt-in does not store an A/B note. | Check raw stamps across the complete combined pool and record the stated exception. |
| MAJOR | [guide §5.5.4](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:408), [grid rule](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/scripts/exp_meta_config_grid.py:321), and [serialized rule](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/scripts/exp_meta_config_grid.py:351) disagree on futility and omit alternatives when reference wins. | Require equivalence CIs for every relevant contrast and synchronize the declarations and artifacts. |
| MAJOR | [grid null](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/runs/EXP_META_CONFIG_GRID.md:46), [grid interpretation](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/runs/EXP_META_CONFIG_GRID.md:119), [PROGRESS §20](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/PROGRESS_BRANCH.md:635), and [JSON payload definition](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/scripts/exp_meta_config_grid.py:348) retain raw-slope primary wording or 87% I². | State the standardized null and corrected primary numbers throughout; label 30.87/0.87 secondary. |
| MINOR | [grid §8.2](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/runs/EXP_META_CONFIG_GRID.md:162) still recommends an immediately usable baseline; [screen §6.3](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/runs/EXP_META_CONFIG_SCREEN.md:128) leaves a Rastrigin significance statement unqualified. | Mark the baseline as a held-out candidate and the screen statement as a retracted within-block result. |
| MINOR | [table parser](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/tests/test_boundary_registry.py:49) counts only matching headers and checks only the first four header cells. | Require exactly four header cells and detect any second table in §2.4. |
| MINOR | [guide §5.4](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:377) still describes closed-loop success as a CI excluding zero, which admits a negative result despite §5.5.2. | Say the CI lower bound must exceed zero. |

## C. Standing-spec judgment

The conditionality signal remains present under the exploratory uncertainty check, and the P3 and closed-loop rule corrections are substantive. The package is **not yet fit as the standing modification specification**: its loader boundary can still be bypassed, its futility rule remains internally inconsistent, and several authoritative report passages disagree with the revised primary estimand. I inspected code and saved artifacts only; I did not run tests or training.

VERDICT: REVISE
